          "id": 719322151,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "```\nphton64(aad + 13, decoder->seq);    /* record sequence number */\nphton16(aad + 13, decoder->epoch);  /* DTLS 1.2 includes epoch. */\n```\n\nThe epoch - 2 bytes comes first,\nThe seqn - 6 bytes comes afterwards,\n\nOr is that a trick, to write 8 bytes first, and then overwrite the first 2 bytes of that?\n\nIf so, looks got to me, at least from source without being able to test :-).",
          "author": {
